Excerpts from netnews.rec.games.hack: 9-Sep-93 mid-to-late game
observatio.. by Dan Pritts@css.itd.umich 
> so anyway, i have the bell, book, and candelabrum.   i haven't (duhh)
> found the vib square yet though.  Killing the wiz occasionally hasn't been
> a problem, but it's getting to be a hassle having my shit randomly cursed
> (i presume the book does that?).

Actually, the mere act of killing the Wizard throws the game into what I
think of as the final stage.  This is when speed is what counts.  At
this point, it doesn't matter if you miss a couple of nifty items here
or there.  Just getting the Amulet of Yendor and hauling booty the
endgame should be the only thing you are concerned about.

Incidentally, before I mess with the Wizard at all I map out all of the
staircases in hell as well as locating the vibrating square (and marking
it by dropping one gold piece on the eight adjacent squares, which makes
it difficult to miss).  That way, when I kill the wizard, I can make
tracks down to visit the High Priest of Moloch.  Use one of those wands
of teleportation that you should be neck deep in and just teleport to
all of the down staircases ["z", ">", ".", ">", "z", ">", ".", ">"...].

> What items would you recommend for my run for the amulet and for my run
> for the endgame?  Should I prepare for the endgame before I go for the
> amulet?

The more you futz around, the more your stuff will get cursed.  Although
it seems like just a pain, things can get kind of touch and go when you
start running out of holy water.

> Do I have to take my gold out with me to get points for it, or can
> i leave it in my chest?  Is it to my advantage to arrange for the
> priest who has ~50k of my gold to have an accident so i can carry that
> gold out?  

You've got to carry it out to get points for it.  I'd say "no" on the
killing the priest...to do so, you'd not only make your god mad (not a
good idea since prayer can sometimes get you out of sticky spots) but
you'd have to go out of your way down the Gnomish mines.

> can i level teleport into the endgame once i've been there?  I'm thinking
> of going into the endgame, clearing it out, level teleporting out to 
> my chest, and then teleporting back with a load of gems.  

You cannot level teleport at all once you have the Amulet, and you
cannot level teleport to the endgame in any case (matter o' fact, I'm
not sure if you can level teleport in the endgame at all...I don't think
there is any way to leave at all).

> I'm thinking piles of blank blessed and cursed (any reason to leave any
> uncursed?) scrolls, and a bunch of magic markers.  I do have my WoW with
> 4 or 5 charges left in case i get in a fix.  I also have two spare amulets
> of life saving, a couple spare rings of teleport control (never got the
> intrinsic), two blessed scrolls of genocide (would genociding elementals
> be a good idea?).  
>
> A bunch of holy and unholy water seems like a good idea too.
>  
> anything else I'm missing?

You NEED, repeat, NEED a ring of levitation.  Not only does this save
you some aggrivation in trying to leave hell with the amulet (it seems
that the "mysterious force" doesn't act on you as often when you are
levitating) but you need it to navigate on the plane of air (okay, you
CAN make progress without it, but it is just a heck of alot easier with
it).  Aside from that, cursed scrolls of gold detection are useful (they
detect traps, but report them as gold) for finding the magic portals.  A
spellbook of remove curse is very useful, and those wands of digging and
teleportation will help in making tracks out of the dungeon.  Don't
forget to wear the Amulet once on the elemental planes...it helps detect
magic portals.

